            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0131" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee (Arms)/115b:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-03-02T14:00:00-05:00">March 2, 1935—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. We are at a loss to understand the attitude of the British Delegation at
                    Geneva toward important elements of our Draft Convention on Arms Manufacture and
                    Trade and would appreciate receiving your analysis as to the motives for this
                    stand and as to the likelihood of its modification in the course of further
                    discussion.</p>
                <p>Please repeat this telegram and your reply to Amdelgat Geneva.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
